The message represents the the response of an llm model, it's received in chunks and append to the message content.
Review the strategy so we make sure vue components react to content changes.
Evaluate if we can safe from recomputing all message all the time.
Suggest improvements keeping in mind reactivity.

## Analysis & Pre-Thinking

- **Core Requirements**: 
  1. Understand how streamed content is appended to `message.content`
  2. Identify reactivity issues with frequent re-parsing of entire message
  3. Ensure Vue components react to content changes without unnecessary recomputation
  4. Keep the `finished` flag fix aligned with actual streaming behavior

- **Strategic Approach**:
  1. Content is appended incrementally via `currentMessage.content += message.content` on each stream chunk
  2. Each re-parse of the entire content causes re-rendering of all blocks (expensive)
  3. Solution: Only re-parse when closing fence is found OR message is complete
  4. Track "last parsed position" to parse only new content
  5. Cache completed blocks; only update last block if open
  6. Align `finished` flag with actual completion (when `event_type === 'done'`)

- **Dependencies & Risks**:
  - Vue reactivity: Assigning to array elements should trigger updates (Vue 3 behavior)
  - Performance: Current approach re-parses entire message on every chunk (O(n²) behavior)
  - Streaming state: Components need to know if message is still streaming to avoid marking blocks as finished prematurely
  - Risk: Incremental parsing could miss edge cases where fence is split across chunks

- **Target Files**:
  - `src/utils/markdownParser.js` - Add incremental parsing logic
  - `src/components/document/Document.vue` - Only re-parse when necessary
  - `src/components/document/ChapterBlock.vue` - Watch for block changes more efficiently
  - (Optional) `src/store` - Consider caching parsed chapters if using Vuex/Pinia

